# Security policy

## Reporting

Report suspected vulnerabilities privately to {{ owners }} {% if repository_platform == 'github' %}using GitHub private vulnerability reporting or the team's approved security channel{% else %}through the team's approved private security channel{% endif %}. Do not include secrets, exploit payloads, personal data, or unredacted production logs in a public work item.

## Required engineering controls

- Treat all external input and agent/tool output as untrusted data.
- Keep credentials out of source, prompts, logs, fixtures, and committed agent configuration.
- Use least-privilege pipeline permissions and immutable external workflow references.{% if repository_platform == 'github' %} GitHub Actions are pinned to full commit SHAs.{% else %} Central Azure Pipeline templates are pinned to full commit SHAs.{% endif %}
{% if repository_platform == 'azure-devops' and security_profile == 'hardened' %}- Keep Azure DevOps Code Security, Secret Protection, and secret push protection enabled; the repository auditor verifies that external state.
{% endif -%}
- Update and commit the configured SBOM after dependency changes; CI validates its package identities.
- Use `.agent-standard/waivers.json` only for time-bounded, owned exceptions with a concrete reason.

## Supported versions

Until the project publishes a release policy, only the default branch is supported.
